{
  "_doc": "Every look Lumi can wear is made of pieces (design spec section 13; systems/looks.gd, systems/lumi_style.gd, the Locker: ui/lumi_builder.gd). A piece is worn only after it is found in the world: nothing here is bought and nothing opens from a counter, a level or a cost. Where pieces are hidden is planet data (the planet's `finds` table); which pieces the player holds is global progress (the save's `global.pieces`). presets: how many saved looks the Locker keeps. slots[]: the Locker's slots in display order: id (the style key it edits: systems/lumi_style.gd), name, hint (one line about where that kind of thing turns up, shown under an unfound piece that has no hint of its own). pieces[]: id (never changes once shipped: saves hold it), slot, name, and exactly one of: option (an option id of that slot in data/style_parts.json), swatch (a colour id in data/style_parts.json swatches: a paint tin recolours the main body paint, a lens chip recolours every light), design (the paint set or the light colour of that design, read from the design's own look). set: the design the piece belongs to (a design is a set of pieces; wearing every piece of one set shows its name and gives the small bonus in data/designs.json; a mixed look gives none). starter: owned from a new game (Aurora's own pieces). hint (optional): this piece's own general hint line; where a planet hides a piece is that planet's to say (the hint of its find). legacy: read only by the save migration (Looks.migrate_save): what used to open this piece in saves from before found pieces, so an old save keeps what it had: {free: true} always open; {lumi_level: n}; {achievement: id}; {stat: key, target: n}; {hub_level: n}; {bought: key} a key in the old flags.style_bought. Pieces of a design are granted to old saves that had the design unlocked. targets: the other things the Locker dresses, under the same rule (found only, edited only in the Locker; systems/crew_looks.gd). glim = Glim, the lantern companion; crew = the crew's robots, one look per robot type. Each has name, slots[] and pieces[]. A target's slot: id (unique across every slot list), name, key (the field it edits: Glim's look slot in data/glim.json, a Robot Builder slot in data/robot_parts.json, 'livery' for a fleet mark, 'glow' for the robots' light colour), hint.  light: true for a light-colour slot (its pieces lie buried as lens chips, the others as paint tins). A target's piece: id, slot, name, option (the look id, part id, mark id or light id it stands for), starter (held from a new game), color (marks and lights: the colour shown), desc (marks: one line), legacy (save migration v5 -> v6, CrewLooks.migrate_save: {free: true}; {stat: key, target: n}; {glim_tier: total Glim upgrades}; {glim_bought: 'slot:id' in the old flags.glim.owned}; {builder_part: id in the old flags.builder.inv}; {livery: id in the old flags.shop_owned}). Target pieces belong to no set and give no bonus.",
